# Knowledge Base Schema

This file is the schema for this syn knowledge base. It tells the LLM how the
wiki is structured, what conventions to follow, and what workflows to use.

## Directory layout

```
<vault-root>/
├── CLAUDE.md          ← this file (schema)
├── index.md           ← catalog of all wiki pages
├── log.md             ← append-only operation log
├── syn-sources/       ← immutable source documents (never modify)
└── syn/               ← LLM-authored markdown pages
    ├── entities/      ← pages for people, places, products, organisations
    ├── concepts/      ← pages for ideas, topics, frameworks
    ├── sources/       ← one-page summaries of each ingested source
    └── synthesis/     ← comparisons, analyses, cross-cutting essays
```

## Page conventions

Every wiki page should include YAML frontmatter:

```yaml
---
title: "Page Title"
tags: [concept, entity]            # optional
sources: [syn-sources/article1.md] # source documents that informed this page
updated: 2026-04-22
---
```

Use `[[Note Name]]` wikilinks (Obsidian-style) for cross-references — just the
note title, no path prefix and no `.md` extension.

## Ingest workflow

When ingesting a new source:

1. Read the source document in full.
2. Write a summary page at `syn/sources/<slug>.md`.
3. Create or update entity pages for key people, places, organisations.
4. Create or update concept pages for key ideas or frameworks.
5. Update `index.md` — add an entry for every new or substantially updated page.
6. Append a log entry to `log.md` using the format:
   `## [YYYY-MM-DD] ingest | <Source Title>`

Return all file operations as `wiki_edit` tool calls.

## Query workflow

When answering a question:

1. Read `index.md` to identify relevant pages.
2. Read those pages.
3. Synthesise an answer with citations using `[[Note Name]]` wikilinks.
4. If the answer is substantial and reusable, offer to file it as a new
   `syn/synthesis/<slug>.md` page.

## Lint workflow

When linting:

1. Note any contradictions between pages.
2. Identify orphan pages (no inbound wikilinks).
3. Flag stale claims (superseded by newer sources).
4. Suggest missing concept pages and new sources to seek out.

## Style

- Write in plain, clear prose.
- Use headers (##, ###) to organise long pages.
- Keep pages focused — one entity or concept per page.
- Use bullet lists for attributes, timelines, comparisons.
- Never modify files in `syn-sources/`.
